# Cuttlely project notes

Project notes live in `.projects/cuttlely/` and ship with the repository. They are public.

- Read `.projects/cuttlely/README.md` and `.projects/cuttlely/STATUS.md` before other work, and continue from that state. A new person runs the `take-over` skill.
- `.projects/cuttlely/DECISIONS.md` is settled. Do not reinvent it; supersede a decision with a new entry and a reason.
- Use `.projects/cuttlely/RUNBOOK.md` for commands and gotchas, `MEMORY.md` for conventions, `PLAN.md` for the next tasks, `OPEN.md` for blockers, and `ARTIFACTS.md` for where docs, samples, and fixtures live.
- When project state changes, update the affected files in `.projects/cuttlely/` in the same change. To refresh the notes and agent files against git, run the `refresh-project-handoff` skill.
- Keep the notes public-safe: no secrets, personal names or accounts, private hosts, internal links, machine paths, customer data, or business notes. Link issues instead of restating their status.
- If `.projects/cuttlely/` is missing from a checkout (a stripped export), follow the root `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, and `CONTRIBUTING.md`. Do not invent the notes.
- Never commit or print secrets (model keys, tokens, `.cuttlely/`, `.env`).

- Inbound API/SDK changes follow `docs/reference/access-keys.md`: explicit resource/operation grants, preserved legacy values, separate provider/share transports, and the access-key execution fixtures. `INBOUND_ACCESS_V2` defaults to `off`.

- Current work: Import & verify on `main` after the 1.7.3 release (`11fab773`). Imported test stamps are not ready. A required empty credential can be chosen and blocks Ready until then. A new canvas adopts the created flow and its draft status, and does not show imported cards when that status cannot be loaded. An imported stamp blocks Publish until a verification record exists. A running check keeps a newer same-user draft. A new agent team saves its imported file as a draft. A contract with no query name is not Ready. A missing required connection, an empty report or CSV, a contract that does not name one tested query, or a check that stops early keeps Publish off. A running check with no live job can be resumed. Credential choices require credentials:view. Verification stays on the draft. Read all ten handoff files completely in contiguous pages before edits and retain observed page text and coverage evidence. Follow STATUS and RUNBOOK for facts.
- Read `docs/upgrading.md` and `docs/how-to/instance-operator.md`: security-exception warnings, operator-only service settings, host-log proof from the hosting dashboard or Docker/Compose logs, and enforcement default Off. Public figures in `docs/images/access-keys/` retain product 1.6.1 / feature head `5c08b125` provenance; AK02/06/08/09 stay pending.

- Historical 1.7.1 maintenance preparation adds validated flow-first key presets, view-level scoped Harness execution, private copies, a controlled saved-access selector and real migrated-Postgres deletion coverage. STATUS records complete-read provenance and focused evidence. Publication and activation stay separate; use the exact final-head full gate and retain 1.7.0 upgrade/recovery requirements.
